# Waterfall, climbed on Route 210 North after surfing out to the foot of it.
#
# The tile came out of the compiled map data, not out of a scan. A land-data
# member is four sizes and then 32x32 terrain attributes, one u16 a tile whose
# low byte is the behaviour, and the map matrices say which member sits at
# which 32x32 cell of the world. Reading those two together says where every
# waterfall in the game is: eight of the 666 members carry behaviour 0x13 at
# all, 55 tiles between them, which is why scanning the window around two
# dozen warps found none of them.
#
# The player starts on the bank facing the river, so the run has to surf out
# first: two field moves in one station, and the second is the one no other
# station reaches.

name FALLS
gender GENDER_MALE
trainer-id 30010
money 3000
badge BADGE_ID_FEN
badge BADGE_ID_BEACON
party SPECIES_BIBAREL 30 ITEM_NONE
party-move 0 0 MOVE_SURF
party-move 0 1 MOVE_WATERFALL
map MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_210_NORTH 504 527 FACE_RIGHT
